Fix: the "too few processor cores" warning is said once, not at every affinity change

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0020-few-cores-warn-once.patch
Status:     upstream log-spam bug (report to rexglue-sdk)

WHAT BROKE
  On a PC with fewer than 6 logical processors (a 2-core / 4-thread laptop
  CPU), a game log of 8 minutes held 163,671 lines, 162,000 of them the same
  warning: "Too few processor cores - scheduling will be wonky". About 300
  lines per second, from the game's D3D thread and another guest thread.

WHY
  XThread::SetActiveCpu (src/system/xthread.cpp) pins the host thread to the
  guest's core only with 6+ logical processors, and otherwise logged the
  warning. It runs for every KeSetAffinityThread, and Crash: Mind over
  Mutant's D3D code moves its threads between cores constantly. Each line is a
  formatted log write on a thread the game is waiting for, on exactly the PCs
  with the least CPU to spare.

FIX
  The warning is said once per run (std::atomic flag) and names the core
  count. Behaviour is unchanged: affinities are still ignored below 6.

HOW IT WAS FOUND
  A player's log from a 4-thread PC (lag spikes while streaming) was 16 MB;
  sorting its lines by message showed the one warning.

diff --git a/src/system/xthread.cpp b/src/system/xthread.cpp
index 77bce25..6052693 100644
--- a/src/system/xthread.cpp
+++ b/src/system/xthread.cpp
@@ -899,7 +899,14 @@ void XThread::SetActiveCpu(uint8_t cpu_index) {
       thread_->set_affinity_mask(uint64_t(1) << cpu_index);
     }
   } else {
-    REXSYS_WARN("Too few processor cores - scheduling will be wonky");
+    // Said ONCE: games re-pin threads constantly (Crash: Mind over Mutant ~300 calls/s), and on a
+    // 4-thread PC this line alone filled 160,000 log lines in 8 minutes, each a formatted file write
+    // on the busy threads.
+    static std::atomic<bool> warned{false};
+    if (!warned.exchange(true)) {
+      REXSYS_WARN("Too few processor cores ({} logical, 6 needed) - guest thread affinities are ignored "
+                  "(said once)", rex::thread::logical_processor_count());
+    }
   }
 }
 
